# Strong types

## JS/TS

- ALWAYS `effect/Schema` at boundaries: `Schema.Struct` and
  `Schema.decodeUnknown`. Prefer `typeof schema.Type` over a second hand-written
  interface for the same payload.
- NEVER Zod. NEVER `any`. NEVER non-null assertions (`!`). NEVER `as` to brand
  or accept unvalidated data. `as const` on a literal is fine.

## Rust

- ALWAYS newtypes and validated constructors for domain ids. See
  `020-no-shortcuts-rust`.

## Python

- ALWAYS annotate parameters and return values. basedpyright `strict` must pass.
  See `020-python`.
